{"kind":"request","text":"XD-1: exact-revision submit for drafts. Hugh, 21 November, from dap-foldkit: the application checks a draft's key before submit, but another tab can edit the content under the same key before the client takes its first submission fence, so the member signs content they did not review.\nApply the patch at ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-21-exact-draft/exact-draft.patch (SHA-256 e256fb09a96032dd89aea6be52c7705fe6b7d7ccce0d6562e575a620d5e51f61, prepared on 95ec0456; git apply --check passes on 02d93554). It adds `revision` (a digest of the canonical stored draft) to DraftContent, and an optional third argument to ScopeClient.submit(slot, now, revision). At the first fence, after `taken` and before signing, a stored revision that differs stops with `draft-changed`. Two-argument callers are unchanged.\nPlanner review of the patch: the check sits at the right step, a malformed revision stops with `shape` before any await, and no application or package switches over DraftStop, so the widened union breaks no caller. The revision changes on any stored change, including a return; that is intended (the exact stored draft), and the member reads the new view.\nAdd, in the same head: the developer guide's draft section names `revision` and `draft-changed` and tells an application to show the updated draft and ask the member to review it. The patch's regression test stays.","body":{"conditions":"Patch applied as given plus the guide paragraph; client typecheck and the c4-draft-now suite; one full gate, alone or batched with a group that does not touch packages/client, next after the security group; checker review (Architecture, Security, Simplification); the dap-foldkit change follows in that repository after this lands.","target_head":"02d93554957be876a33297cfd0d9cd693046dea2","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}